"Run dir: /Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/e2e/20261018T064404Z-pre1/ (steps.json, logs/, pdf/, pdf/real/). Final result: 30 PASS, 0 FAIL, 0 NOT_RUN. The Bends & order step went entirely through the UI, so the API fallback was never used.\n\n**What was already there.** `scripts/production/run_e2e_app.mjs` already drove step 5 through Vendor Setup when I picked it up. It opens it from the wizard's \"Tag bends\" button, clicks each auto-marked bend on the model and confirms it, tags the order, groups bends into a \u05de\u05d4\u05dc\u05da, toggles folded/unfolded, saves, clicks \"Done, back to the wizard\", and only then checks the API. The old PUT vendor-setup path survives only as a fallback that records FAIL. VendorSetupPage already had every hook it needs, so I made no edits there.\n\n**What I changed:**\n1. **Station live stream fix** (`frontend/react/src/features/station/hooks/useStationFeed.ts`). The server closes the station's live event stream every 5 minutes. The client then waited 15 s before reconnecting, so the kiosk showed \"Polling\" for 15 s each time. Now a stream that was healthy for at least 30 s reopens after 1 s, and the station re-reads its feed when the stream closes and when it reopens. That re-read is needed because events sent between the two streams are not replayed. My intermediate run without it (20261018T063646Z-pre1) failed R4: the real job reached the station 10.9 s after finishing, over the 5 s limit. tsc and eslint pass.\n2. **New informational check in R4** (`run_e2e_app.mjs`): the station must be on the live stream when the real job is shown. In the final run it was live, and the stream reopened 1 s after the server closed it.\n\n**Per-step result (20261018T064404Z-pre1):**\n- **S0\u2013S2: PASS.** App copy built with `--profile app` into the temp dir; server refuses to start without SECRET_KEY (exit 2); admin, server and line service started; readiness OK.\n- **W1\u2013W3: PASS.** Login, new part, STEP upload (4 auto-marked bends), PDF drawing.\n- **W4: PASS, through the UI.** All 8 bend clicks landed on the model (none fell back to the list). The 4 list rows match the 4 API bends and the 4 markers. The order was set to B1, B4, B2, B3 with two \u05de\u05d4\u05dc\u05da groups, [B1, B4] and [B2, B3]. The studio's folded/unfolded toggle worked; before the flat is uploaded its unfolded view comes from the CAD. The API showed the draft (revision 1), all bends confirmed, matching order and groups, and the order confirmed; the wizard showed 4/4 marks reviewed.\n- **W5, W6, W6b: PASS.** Flat binding confirmed; the unfolded view comes from the uploaded flat in both the wizard and the studio; studio in Hebrew RTL.\n- **W7\u2013W9: PASS.** Tolerances, release as SKU@v1, expectations table and benchmark row, wizard in Hebrew RTL.\n- **K1\u2013K11: PASS.** All station steps passed. K2 injected errors: B2 flange FAIL at 53.47 (truth 53.5) and B3 angle FAIL at 92.05\u00b0 (truth 92\u00b0); the station updated 0.38 s after the job finished.\n- **R1\u2013R5: PASS (real 10839000).**\n  - **R1:** its STEP and FULL scan went in as read-only, byte-identical copies, and the solver auto-marked 12 bends.\n  - **R2:** done through the UI, with all 24 clicks on the model and \u05de\u05d4\u05dc\u05da [B1, B2].\n  - **R3:** released as 10839000@v1.\n  - **R4:** the job completed in 19 s. Result: inspection VALID, OUT_OF_TOLERANCE_FOUND, 48 measurements taken; station updated 0.1 s after the job finished.\n  - **R5:** worst-first, station in Hebrew, 8-page PDF.\n- **Z1: PASS.** No page errors.\n\nHebrew PDF check: \"\u05dc\u05d0 \u05d4\u05d5\u05db\u05e8\u05e2\" appears in reading order (not only mirrored) and the running header is correct on every page.\n\n**Superseded runs (kept on disk):**\n- 20261018T062339Z-pre1: 30 PASS, before the station fix.\n- 20261018T063646Z-pre1: 28 PASS, R4 FAIL (10.9 s), R5 NOT_RUN.\n\n**Open issues (outside apps/** and frontend features; not fixed):**\n1. **Engine, real 10839000:** B1/B2 come out PARTIALLY_FORMED. B2's flange A and B look swapped (3.75 measured against 21.41 nominal, and 20.24 against 3.61), and its bend-line offset is +17.3. B8 flange A is 3.71 against 21.41. The 90\u00b0 bends read about 1.2\u20132.0\u00b0 under nominal across the board, which may be a measurement bias or real springback.\n2. **PDF report (`domains/production/reporting`):** the bends row says \"formed 12\" while the same report says \"partially formed bend found\" and B1/B2 are PARTIALLY_FORMED. Partially formed bends are being counted as formed.\n3. **CAD unfold:** for the real 10839000 STEP the studio says \"Unfolding is unavailable for this CAD geometry\", so the folded/unfolded toggle was not exercised on the real part (recorded as informational). It is covered on the synthetic part (W4, W6, W6b).\n4. **Leftover processes:** about 7 server/service pairs from earlier runs (started 17 Oct, 9:42 PM to 1:25 AM, from temp app copies) are still running. I did not stop them because they are not from this run. This run's temp dir was removed.\n\n**Screenshots** (each paired with a DOM/API assertion, in /Users/idantal/ShermanQC/FullProject/docs/production/runlog/e2e/20261018T064404Z-pre1/):\n01-production-parts.png, 02-new-part-form.png, 03-wizard-cad.png, 04-wizard-drawing.png, 05-w4-bends-entry.png, 06-w4-studio-auto-marked.png, 07-w4-studio-confirmed.png, 08-w4-studio-order-moves.png, 09-w4-studio-unfolded.png, 10-w4-studio-folded.png, 11-w4-studio-saved.png, 12-w4-wizard-bends-order.png, 13-wizard-flat-proposal.png, 14-wizard-flat-confirmed.png, 15-wizard-unfolded.png, 16-wizard-folded.png, 17-studio-unfolded-from-flat.png, 18-studio-folded-again.png, 19-studio-hebrew-rtl.png, 20-wizard-tolerances.png, 21-wizard-review.png, 22-wizard-released.png, 23-wizard-released-expectations.png, 24-wizard-hebrew-rtl.png, 25-station-token-gate.png, 26-station-connected.png, 27-station-in-progress.png, 28-station-result-errors.png, 29-station-heatmap-off